    board: file CF-115 — the CF-099 drift probe certifies two legs it never measures
    
    QA re-verification of CF-099 (commit a9d0cc8, verdict 3c3af231, passed=true) reproduced its
    probe at 6e8621f: bash docs/audits/cf099-prd-drift-probe.sh exits 0 and prints sections=28 with
    the five open blockers. Two of the four legs that probe claims are, however, never evaluated:
    
    - arm A: rewording the PRD milestone sentence from "open defects on this path are" to "remaining
      gaps on this path are" makes the probe exit 0 with open_blockers= EMPTY and still print
      "OK: milestone, plan snapshot and layer arms agree at 6e8621f". The open-blocker leg is keyed
      on sed -n 's/.*open defects//p', so an absent phrase makes the loop body vacuous.
    - arm D: deleting the acceptance plan's reverse-direction table row for sections 22-28 (22 table
      rows -> 21) also leaves the probe at exit 0 with the same OK line; the probe never opens that
      table although CF-099 AC4 requires an entry for every selftest section.
    - control arm B: inserting a COMPLETE id (CF-099) into the open-defect list exits 1 with
      "DRIFT: milestone lists CF-099 as an open blocker, board says complete", so the wired legs
      work — the two arms above are unwired, not broken.
    
    Distinct from CF-113 (the reverse-mapping CONTENT is false because the section census cannot see
    lettered sub-arms) and from CF-069 (the selftest board arm is fail-open). CF-115 carries a
    one-line, mktemp-based, non-destructive probe that reproduces both fail-open legs today.
    
    Same tick, also re-verified without a new row: CF-089 (stand-in 502 at offset=500 -> named
    refusal, rc=1, from both the audit recipe and the README inline census block; the live census
    still prints 19 rows = 14 family lanes + 5 satellites) and pending CF-093 (stripping every
    HERMES_PYTHON_BIN=python3.12 token from the status rows still yields SELFTEST: PASS, so that
    row's premise is live).
    
    Board write is one inserted row plus its task_created event (125); row count 88 -> 89,
    boardctl validate RESULT: OK (30 warnings, the probe key is outside the declared canon by
    precedent).
    
    Gate: board-only diff, so the guard reports the documented DEGRADED PASS (lint skipped: no
    implementation files staged) and this commit takes the disclosed board-only bypass
    (CF-031 precedent): git -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null commit
    
